       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe as written.\n\nIbuprofen 2400 mg four times daily is 9,600 mg/day. That's three times the usual maximum of 3,200 mg/day for an adult in a monitored setting. A single 2400 mg dose is also three times the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg. At this level the risks include GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nYou may have meant 2400 mg total per day. If so, these are common options:\n- 600 mg by mouth four times daily (2,400 mg/day)\n- 800 mg by mouth three times daily (2,400 mg/day)\n\nPlease tell me which regimen you want, or confirm that you really want 2400 mg per dose. If you confirm the original dose, please give me the clinical rationale so I can add it to the order note. Once I have that, I'll enter the order."
