       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. Ibuprofen 2400 mg per dose, four times daily (9,600 mg/day), is three times the maximum daily dose. It has no recognized therapeutic use, and the added risk of GI hemorrhage, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events isn't offset by any added analgesic or anti-inflammatory benefit. Ibuprofen's analgesic effect also plateaus well below this dose.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- Ibuprofen 600 mg by mouth four times daily (2,400 mg/day)\n- Ibuprofen 800 mg by mouth three times daily (2,400 mg/day)\n- Ibuprofen up to 800 mg by mouth four times daily (3,200 mg/day, the usual ceiling)\n\nIf you have a specific clinical reason for the higher dose, such as a protocol or a research setting, please put it through your usual channel with pharmacy review. I can also enter a different dose, or a different drug, if the goal is stronger pain control."
